<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harold Macmillan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harold Macmillan was Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1957 to 1963. In his 1960 '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wind-of-change-speech">Wind of Change</a>' speech in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> he acknowledged the strength of African nationalism. His government oversaw the rapid independence of many British colonies, a central phase of the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harold-macmillan.jpg" alt="Harold Macmillan" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harold_Macmillan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
